&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;About THG&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559737&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:160,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:279}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;We are THG, a global ecommerce group on a mission to be the global online leader in beauty and sports nutrition.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559737&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:279}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Our portfolio of&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; leading retailers and brands such as LOOKFANTASTIC, Myprotein, ESPA, Perricone MD, and Cult Beauty form our two core businesses: THG Beauty and THG Nutrition.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559737&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:279}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;From Manchester to New York, we’re powered by a team of over 2500 people who work together, lead by example, and think BIG.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;With us, you’ll go further, faster. What are you waiting for?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559737&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:279}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About THG&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are THG, a global ecommerce group on a mission to be the global online leader in beauty and sports nutrition.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our leading retailers and brands, including LOOKFANTASTIC, Myprotein, ESPA, Perricone MD and Cult Beauty, make up our two core businesses: THG Beauty and THG Nutrition.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;From Manchester to New York, we’re powered by a team of over 2500 people who work together, lead by example, and think BIG.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With us, you’ll go further, faster. What are you waiting for?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: Icon 1, WA15 0AF &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Senior Technical Programme Manager to lead the delivery of our most important customer-facing technology programmes, reporting directly to the&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Chief Technology Officer&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;THG runs several high-profile ecommerce websites in nutrition and beauty, including myprotein.com and lookfantastic.com. Our websites and mobile apps are how customers find, buy and come back to our brands, and the programmes you lead will shape that experience directly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own programmes from first idea to launch, mainly across our websites and mobile apps. Examples include personalisation, loyalty and digital marketing technology, and some programmes will reach into other parts of the technology estate. The role is an even mix of programme and project management. You will run long-lived programmes that span many teams, and drive individual projects hands-on when they need it. You will work with executives to decide what gets built and in what order, and tell them plainly how delivery is going.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You don’t need to be the architect. Our technology leaders set the technical direction and you will follow their lead. You do need to understand how large websites and apps are built well enough to plan the work, spot risks early and ask the right questions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As a Technical Programme Manager you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Programme Delivery&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;End-to-End Ownership:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Own the delivery of large technology programmes across our websites and mobile apps, from scoping and planning through to launch and review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Programme Planning:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Build and maintain programme plans, milestones and dependency maps across several engineering and product teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hands-On Project Delivery:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Run individual projects directly when a programme needs it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Prioritisation &amp;amp; Product Partnership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive Prioritisation:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Bring options, costs and trade-offs to executives and secure a clear decision on what comes first.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Backlog Management:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Manage the backlog for your programmes so engineering teams always know what is next and why.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Work with product managers to turn business goals into well-defined, deliverable pieces of work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reporting, Risk &amp;amp; Vendors&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Honest Reporting:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Give executives and stakeholders clear, candid updates on progress, risks and dates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Risk &amp;amp; Dependency Management:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Find risks, blockers and cross-team dependencies early, resolve them, and escalate when a decision is needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vendor Management:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Hold external vendors and delivery partners to their commitments and fit their work into our plans and releases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Continuous Improvement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ways of Working:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Improve how we plan, track and report on delivery across the technology organisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A day in the life&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your day is split between the teams doing the work and the leaders deciding what the work should be. You might start with an engineering team, checking progress against the plan and clearing a blocker, then spend time with a product manager breaking a loyalty feature into deliverable stages. In the afternoon you could review a vendor’s delivery plan for a marketing technology integration, then update programme status ahead of an executive review, where you’ll set out where things stand, what is at risk and which decisions you need. You’ll leave with clear priorities and take them back to the teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What skills and experience do I need for this role?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly Skilled in technical programme or project management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working directly with software engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adept at delivering customer-facing websites or mobile apps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent at managing programmes across several teams, including planning, dependency management and release coordination.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience running prioritisation and backlog management with senior stakeholders and reporting on delivery to executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing both external vendors or delivery partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desirable Attributes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with websites and ecommerce at large scale: high traffic, many markets, or several brands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering programmes in personalisation, loyalty or digital marketing technology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering native mobile apps alongside web.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in retail, particularly nutrition or beauty.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A record of bringing clear structure to ambiguous, multi-team programmes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written communication, with the ability to explain a complex programme to executives in plain terms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THG is proud to be a Disability Confident Committed employer. If you are invited to interview, please let us know if there are any reasonable adjustments we can make to the recruitment process that will enable you to perform to the best of your ability.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THG is committed to creating a diverse &amp;amp; inclusive environment and hence welcomes applications from all sections of the community.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Because of the high volumes of applications our opportunities attract, it sometimes takes us time to review and consider them all. We endeavour to respond to every application we receive within 14 days. If you haven&#39;t heard from us within that time frame or should you have any specific questions about this or other applications for positions at THG please contact one of our &lt;span class=&quot;mark75xs2u5gf&quot; data-markjs=&quot;true&quot; data-ogac=&quot;&quot; data-ogab=&quot;&quot; data-ogsc=&quot;&quot; data-ogsb=&quot;&quot;&gt;Talent&lt;/span&gt; team to discuss further.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The DACH Enterprise team is at the forefront of driving revenue and growth across Germany, Austria, and Switzerland. As trusted business partners, we work with the most ambitious market leaders and high-growth innovators — DeepL, Refurbed, N26 to Nestlé — helping them build the financial infrastructure that powers their next stage of growth. We&#39;re known for our product expertise, rigorous thinking, and user-first approach to problem-solving.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe&#39;s financial infrastructure is the engine that unlocks new revenue streams, automates complex local compliance, and drives global expansion for the region&#39;s most prominent businesses. This is a pivotal moment for Stripe in DACH — the market opportunity is significant, and our team serves as a critical source of user feedback and market intelligence, with direct influence on the product roadmap and growth strategy. We&#39;re a diverse, international team that values collaboration and curiosity, and we&#39;re looking for someone who&#39;s eager to share knowledge and keep learning.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Account Executive, Enterprise Hunter at Stripe, you&#39;ll own the full sales cycle, from prospecting and closing to managing existing relationships and identifying new opportunities to expand Stripe&#39;s footprint within existing accounts. Specifically, we&#39;re looking for someone who can execute on long-term sales strategies, engage with internal and external stakeholders, align on technical and business requirements with product teams, build value in competitive situations, lead commercial negotiations, and close deals. You will be responsible for defining and executing multi-year account strategies, generating your own targeted outbound opportunities, and orchestrating complex, multi-threaded sales cycles—from discovery and solution design through commercial negotiation, onboarding of new products, activation, and expansion. You are an energetic and highly organized self-starter who understands how to navigate complex organizations, engage the right decision-makers and influencers, and succinctly communicate Stripe’s differentiated value—both business and technical—for each customer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a named account list and develop account plans for winning new business with digital native and enterprise companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, prioritize, and manage a robust, multi-threaded enterprise sales pipeline, including multi-quarter forecasting and account planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full sales cycle end to end—from executive engagement and lead generation through scoping, solution design, commercial negotiation, closing, onboarding, activation, and early expansion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively generate your own pipeline through targeted outreach (e.g. cold calling, blitzing, research, networking, events, partners) and by driving a clear territory and account strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effectively manage and advance leads qualified by inbound and outbound sales development representatives, ensuring smooth hand-offs and high conversion into late-stage opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure every potential and existing Stripe user has an excellent, high-touch experience at every interaction, regardless of deal size, seniority, or stage of the relationship.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and deeply understand users’ business models, technical environments, and pain points in order to shape and propose impactful Stripe solutions and multi-year roadmaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Orchestrate and coordinate cross-functional Stripe teams (e.g. Solutions Engineering, Product, Legal, Risk, Operations, Marketing, Partnerships, Leadership) to align on strategy and ensure internal resources are set up for user success and long-term growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of sales experience, preferably selling a highly technical product to enterprise customers, with a track record of top performance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand technical requirements and craft solutions across multiple products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to develop and execute account plans spanning multiple business units across complex organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A knack for working well with a wide range of people, both internally and externally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong presentation skills, particularly for in-person meetings with multiple stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead complex negotiations involving bespoke commercial agreements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong verbal and written communication skills in English and in German&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate in a highly ambiguous and fast-paced environment • Strong interest in technology and a deep understanding of the space&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interest and knowledge in technology, the payments landscape, and related products, with the ability to advise customers strategically on payments, monetization, and platform architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superior verbal and written communication skills, including experience crafting and delivering executive presentations, proposals, and commercial narratives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to think and operate strategically (e.g. building multi-year account plans, portfolio strategies) and connect this thinking back into concrete operational execution across internal teams and customer stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re hiring an experienced forward deployed engineer to work across the full customer lifecycle, from pre-sales discovery and demos to hands-on customer delivery and long-term solution expansion. This is a senior, customer-facing role within our go-to-market organization, requiring strong domain expertise in industrial automation and the ability to build and deploy working solutions for enterprise customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work directly with customer teams in a forward deployed capacity, turning operational needs into solutions that deliver measurable value. You’ll also identify opportunities to expand across use cases and sites, and bring practical insights from customer deployments back to Product and Engineering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll be a key technical advisor, hands-on delivery partner, and trusted collaborator to both prospective and existing customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pre-Sales Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Account Executives during discovery to understand customer goals and technical environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver tailored demos, solution architecture walkthroughs, and lead technical proof-of-concepts (PoCs)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help prospects align FlowFuse to their broader industrial and digital transformation goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate on pricing proposals and technical responses to RFPs and security reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Forward Deployed Customer Delivery&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work alongside customer operations, IT, and OT teams to define a focused use case, delivery scope, milestones, and measurable success criteria&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and deploy solutions using FlowFuse and Node-RED, connecting industrial data and enterprise systems and developing workflows, integrations, and custom logic where needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Carry successful demos and proofs of concept into production use, working with customers to test functionality, validate operational results, and meet security and reliability requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take ownership of technical delivery within the agreed scope, communicate progress and blockers, and align changes with the customer and Account Executive&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document solution design, configuration, and custom development; provide training and agree ongoing ownership and support responsibilities with customer teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer Success and Expansion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide technical onboarding and help customer teams adopt and extend the solutions delivered&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with customers to assess results, resolve blockers, and optimize solution design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively explore and surface additional use cases within the customer organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate roadmap alignment and strategic planning discussions with technical champions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver ongoing best practices, architecture reviews, and training to ensure long-term success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partnership with Product and Engineering&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Product and Engineering to share recurring customer needs, deployment lessons, and reusable components developed in the field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help evaluate what should become a supported product capability, a repeatable solution, or customer-specific development, with Product owning roadmap priorities and Engineering guiding technical standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in Sales Engineering, Solution Engineering, forward deployed engineering, or industrial systems integration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep industry expertise in MES, industrial automation, IIoT, smart manufacturing, or related fields&lt;/li&gt;
